$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=z5fconv  LOC_AFTER=?

* Lean LSeries_convolution' for a finitely supported first factor: if A vanishes off the finite set F of positive integers and B is bounded, then sum_ n ( A * B ) ( n ) n ^ -Z converges to ( sum_ d e. F A ( d ) d ^ -Z ) ( sum_ k B ( k ) k ^ -Z ) for Re Z > 1 (C7b's dconvlim; the log-average bound and the convergence of the A-series come from the finite support).

